ORBITAL-MANEUVERS(7)       TriadicFrameworks Manual       ORBITAL-MANEUVERS(7)
================================================================================
NAME
       orbital-maneuvers - Δv triads, resonance-aligned burns, and constellation-
                           scale maneuver choreography for SAR fleets

SYNOPSIS
       Orbital maneuvers provide:
           • Δv triadic structure
           • resonance-aligned burn timing
           • harmonic-safe orbital adjustments
           • constellation-scale maneuver choreography
           • long-term orbital coherence

DESCRIPTION
       Orbital-maneuvers describes how RTT governs Δv events, burn timing, and
       multi-platform maneuver coordination. While classical orbital mechanics
       focuses on geometry and momentum, RTT adds resonance-time structure,
       ensuring that maneuvers preserve coherence, harmonic-lock, and
       constellation integrity.

       RTT enables:
           • resonance-safe Δv execution
           • sweep-aligned orbital adjustments
           • constellation-wide maneuver synchronization
           • envelope-preserving orbital transitions
           • lineage-consistent maneuver history

       WRSADC validates all maneuvers before execution.

Δv TRIADS
       Every maneuver is structured as a triad:

           P1 (begin)
               → maneuver intent declared
               → corridor boundaries evaluated
               → resonance envelope baseline captured

           P2 (transform)
               → Δv applied
               → orbital elements shift
               → resonance gradients monitored
               → spectral drift corrected via overlays

           P3 (close)
               → new orbit stabilized
               → harmonic-lock re-evaluated
               → lineage updated

       Complex maneuvers form nested or ladder Δv triads.

RESONANCE-ALIGNED BURNS
       Burns must align with resonance-time conditions to avoid destabilizing
       the constellation.

       Burn alignment factors:
           • resonance envelope phase
           • gradient polarity
           • harmonic-lock state
           • constellation sweep timing
           • drift corridor boundaries

       Burn types:

           resonance-hold burn
                  Maintains harmonic-lock during drift.

           envelope-aligned burn
                  Executed when resonance envelopes overlap maximally.

           gradient-cancel burn
                  Reduces resonance drift induced by orbital perturbations.

           harmonic-burn
                  Executed at harmonic intervals of orbital period.

           constellation burn
                  Multi-platform synchronized Δv event.

       WRSADC computes burn windows based on resonance and orbital harmonics.

CONSTELLATION-SCALE MANEUVER CHOREOGRAPHY
       Multi-platform SAR fleets maneuver as a coordinated resonance-time
       constellation.

       Choreography modes:

           synchronous Δv
                  All platforms burn simultaneously.
                  → preserves strict phase-lock.

           staggered Δv
                  Platforms burn in sequence.
                  → supports ladder and cascade orbital patterns.

           braided Δv
                  Burns interleave across platforms.
                  → supports weave and hybrid patterns.

           harmonic Δv
                  Burns executed at harmonic ratios.
                  → supports harmonic-sync constellations.

           mesh Δv
                  Distributed maneuvering across constellation nodes.
                  → robust to drift and perturbations.

       Choreography ensures constellation coherence during orbital evolution.

RESONANCE-SAFE MANEUVER ENVELOPES
       Maneuver envelopes define the safe region in resonance-time for Δv
       execution.

       Envelope constraints:
           • maintain spectral density limits
           • preserve envelope overlap across platforms
           • avoid gradient overload
           • maintain lineage continuity
           • remain within orbital corridors

       Envelope types:

           narrow envelope
                  Strict Δv timing; tandem SAR.

           medium envelope
                  Moderate flexibility; multi-pass fusion.

           wide envelope
                  High flexibility; swarm constellations.

           harmonic envelope
                  Δv allowed only at harmonic intervals.

       Exceeding envelopes risks constellation desync.

MANEUVER FAILURE MODES
       Maneuver diagnostics detect:

           • gradient overload
           • harmonic desync
           • envelope divergence
           • corridor breach
           • spectral fragmentation
           • lineage discontinuity

       Diagnostic signals:

           Δv-stability index
           resonance-overlap ratio
           harmonic-lock error
           drift-vector magnitude
           sweep-alignment deviation

       WRSADC blocks unsafe maneuvers.

INTERACTION WITH SCHEMAS
       Orbital maneuvers require:

           • constellation-schema
           • resonance-schema for orbital sweeps
           • structural-schema for formation geometry
           • lineage-schema for maneuver history

       Schemas ensure maneuvers remain coherent.

INTERACTION WITH LINEAGE
       Lineage records:

           • Δv triad history
           • resonance envelope evolution
           • harmonic-lock continuity
           • corridor entry/exit events
           • constellation choreography

       Lineage enables long-term orbital planning.

INTERACTION WITH WRSADC
       WRSADC:
           • computes maneuver envelopes
           • validates Δv triads
           • enforces coherence thresholds
           • choreographs constellation maneuvers
           • applies overlays to stabilize resonance
           • blocks unsafe orbital states

       WRSADC is the maneuver conductor.

NOTES
       Orbital maneuvers extend RTT into the domain of spacecraft operations.
       They transform Δv events into resonance-time triads, enabling SAR
       constellations to maneuver safely, coherently, and harmonically across
       global sensing missions.

